'''Mitchell’s Fruit Farms Limited''' is a Pakistani food products company headquartered in Lahore, Pakistan. It was founded in 1933 and was acquired by CCL Holding in 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |last=InpaperMagazine |first=From |date=2025-10-20 |title=COMPANY NEWS |url=https://www.dawn.com/news/1949951 |access-date=2026-02-26 |website=Dawn |language=en}}</ref>

==History==
Mitchell's, brainchild of Francis J. Mitchell<ref>{{Cite web |date=2012-08-01 |title=Mitchell's Fruit Farms Limited |url=http://www.brecorder.com/news/4007844 |access-date=2026-02-26 |website=Brecorder |language=en}}</ref> came into existence during the British Indian era near [[Renala Khurd]]. The company was formally registered in [[Lahore]] in April 1933 under the name ''Indian Mildura Fruit Farms Limited''.{{cn|date=February 2026}}

Following the [[Pakistan Movement|independence of Pakistan in 1947]], the company was renamed ''Mitchell’s Fruit Farms Ltd.''{{cn|date=February 2026}} In 1958, Francis Mitchell sold a majority of his shares to Syed Maratib.{{cn|date=February 2026}}

1993, Mitchell's was listed on the [[Karachi Stock Exchange]].<ref name=MS>[https://www.marketscreener.com/quote/stock/MITCHELL-S-FRUIT-FARMS-LI-20704125/company/ Mitchell's business summary and stock quote on MarketScreener.com website] Retrieved 16 December 2020</ref>

== Acquisition by CCL Holding (2025) ==
In 2025, Mitchell’s Fruit Farms Limited entered a new phase of transformation when CCL Holding acquired a majority stake in the company.<ref>{{Cite web |title=MFFL.PK {{!}} Mitchell's Fruit Farms Ltd. Company Profile & Executives - WSJ |url=https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/PK/XKAR/MFFL/company-people |access-date=2026-02-26 |website=www.wsj.com}}</ref>

The acquisition marked a strategic expansion of CCL Holding’s portfolio and reflected its growing focus on the [[Food packaging|food and beverage sector.]]{{cn|date=February 2026}}

== Appointment of key positions ==
Following its acquisition by CCL Holding, Mitchell’s Fruit Farms appointed Kashif Sajjad Sheikh<ref>{{Cite web |title=Governance |url=https://cclpharma.com/governance/ |access-date=2026-02-26 |website=CCL |language=en-US}}</ref> as Chairman and Usman Zafar Butt as Chief Executive Officer<ref>{{Cite web |author=BR Web Desk |date=2025-12-08 |title=Mitchell’s Fruit Farms appoints CEO and chairman following CCL acquisition |url=https://www.brecorder.com/news/40396320 |access-date=2026-02-26 |website=Brecorder |language=en}}</ref>, marking a leadership transition for the company.

